course: dictionary
lesson: 1937
title: Comment: opinions and notes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A comment is something you say or write to give your opinion or to explain something. «He commented on my drawing» means he said something about it, such as what he thought of it.
explain: Comment can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, «a comment» is the remark itself. As a verb, «to comment» means to make such a remark. Teachers write comments on your homework, and you might leave a comment under a video.
explain: Online, a comment is a message people write under a post or video. Some comments are kind and helpful, and some are unkind. Never share personal information in a comment, and report any nasty ones.
fact: A comment can be a spoken remark, a written note, or a message under a post online.
fact: «Comment on» means to say what you think about something: «She commented on the weather.»
fact: Phrases to know: «make a comment», «leave a comment», «no comment».
fact: In computer code, a comment is a note for people that the computer ignores.
fact: Hateful comments about someone's skin colour or religion should be reported, because silence lets hate spread.
exercise: «He commented on my drawing.» What does commented mean here? | Drew a copy of it | Hid it under the table | Forgot it completely | *Said what he thought about it
exercise: In computer code, what is a comment? | A picture of a keyboard | A command the computer must run at once | *A note for people that the computer ignores | A program that writes poems
exercise: A video has a message under it saying «Great work, I loved it!» What is that message? | A script | A password | A title | *A comment
test: Which phrase means you will not say anything about a question? | Make a comment | *No comment | Leave a comment | Comment on it
test: Online, what should you do with a nasty comment? | Copy it into your diary | Share it with your friends | *Report it | Reply with something nastier
exam: Which sentence uses comment as a noun? | She will comment on the film tomorrow. | *She left a comment under the video. | They are commenting now. | He commented loudly in class.
